==German==

===Etymology===
''Kümmel'' is in this case derived from Hebrew ''[[gimel]]'', the third letter of the Hebrew alphabet, and has nothing to do with the spice [[caraway]]. A different name for this game is ''[[Dreiblatt]]'', meaning “three cards”.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|De-Kümmelblättchen.ogg|Audio|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{head|de|noun|g=n}}

# {{lb|de|archaic}} a popular “game”, which is really a set-up scam known as [[three-card monte]], [[Find the Lady]] or [[Bonneteau]].

